       'Run the repeat test: remove every word a stranger outside the sector would not understand or could not repeat (platform, solution, leverage, «AI-powered» without saying what it does) and prefer the concrete noun and verb.',
       'Build the thirty-second version in four beats (what we do, the problem with one vivid fact, the proof, the ask) and the two-minute version in six (hook, problem, solution, proof, why us and why now, the ask).',
       'Adapt per audience: investors hear the size of the change and the traction, customers hear their problem and the result, candidates hear the mission and what they would own.',
       'Offer a high-concept comparison («X for Y») only where it is accurate and flattering in the right way; say what it risks implying.',
